RWKV - https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13048, a very modern RNN, interestingly an almost crowd-sourced science made by volunteers. Linear alternative to transformers, with a very fast inference. However, there aren't any great tutorials or docs, and reimplementing this in PyTorch with a clear tutorial would be very useful. Further versions of RWKV and describing their evolution would also be nice. https://fullstackdeeplearning.com/blog/posts/rwkv-explainer/ - this is a reasonably good resource.